From 744e318babb3f493d7c365bd599ad4ffa7bea1b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Forever Twins v3)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:24:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Forever Twins: v3 helper template (fixed 50/50 fee split,
 simple admin)

Summary
- templates/forever-twin-helper-v3.clar.tmpl: new template for new deployments;
  v2 stays as evidence. Same canonical record, G1/G2 groups and listing guard,
  unpausable swaps, stray-only time-locked rescue and custody read-outs.
- Fee: two payees fixed at deploy (PAYEE-A, PAYEE-B), each paid exactly half.
  Owner may change the fee only to an even amount <= MAX-FEE (u218 if odd).
  A payee inscribing pays only the other payee's half; fee-for quotes exactly
  what charge-fee takes.
- Removed: free threshold, fee-recipient setter and exemption, pause (u211
  retired), one-step transfer-ownership.
- Added: two-step ownership (propose / accept / cancel; u219), interface v3
  with fee, max-fee, payee-a, payee-b, pending-owner.
- scripts/render-helper-v3.mjs: validates payees (standard principals,
  distinct, same network as master), even initial fee <= cap; --example mode
  keeps <PLACEHOLDER> payees and emits undeployable review copies.
- scripts/render-all-v3.mjs, sim/family-suite-v3.mjs, Clarinet.toml entries
  (ft3-*), npm run test:v3; mainnet v3 EXAMPLE configs and rendered review
  copies with <JIM-PAYOUT-ADDRESS> / <RAPHA-PAYOUT-ADDRESS>.

Verification
- family-suite-v3: 341/341 in a scratch simnet (real archived sources for 9
  collections plus mock-leaky-market; Xtrata core replaced by a test double).
  Mutation checks: breaking the split, the even-fee rule, accept-ownership or
  fee-for each makes the suite fail. NOT yet run inside the real harness with
  the real xtrata-v3-2-3; run `npm run test:v3` there.

Notes
- Unaudited prototype; nothing here authorises deployment.
